;
; Put syllable-timed lyrics below as Dialogue lines in the Kara style, set the
; Fontname you want, and run Apply karaoke template. Everything else is
; derived: row positions, row pitch, ruby offset and every clip box follow the
; style's Fontsize, Outline, Shadow and Margins. There are no hardcoded pixels.
;
; TUNING (the config lines just below the styles)
;   emfix       0  size correction between the editor's text measurement and
;                  the renderer. 0 = read it from the font file, which is what
;                  you want. Set a number to pin it. If the named font is NOT
;                  INSTALLED this cannot be read, 1.0 is assumed, and a warning
;                  goes to the automation log: that assumption only holds for
;                  fonts whose lineGap is 0, so install the font.
;   layoutmode     1 = row 1 at the left margin, row 2 right-aligned
;                  2 = centred block, rows nudged apart by indent2
;                  3 = bottom split in half, each row centred in its half
;   rubygap        ruby-to-character gap, px. LOWER = tighter. The visual gap
;                  still varies by font: a font with a small em leaves more
;                  empty space inside the same line box.
;   rubyjust    0  0 = centre ruby on its base. 1 = justify it with \fsp.
;   rowgap         extra clearance between the two rows.
;   minscale   50  floor for auto-fit compression, percent. A line that hits
;                  this floor wants splitting, not squeezing.
;   maxlead  6000  how early a line may appear, row permitting.
;   minlead  1500  GUARANTEED readable time before the wipe. When time is
;                  short the HOLD is sacrificed first, never the lead.
;   postwipe  350  hold after the wipe; shrinks first under pressure.
;   fadein/out     CEILINGS, auto-clamped so the fade-in finishes fadegap ms
;                  before the wipe and the fade-out starts after it ends.
;   nbands      1  1 = flat fill. >1 = vertical gradient slices.
;   gradhf/gradupf vertical span and lift of the gradient, in units of fs.
;   rowy1over/rowy2over  set >0 to override automatic row placement.
;
; COLOURS: unsung is WHITE fill + BLACK outline, sung is COLOURED fill + WHITE
;   outline. The outline flipping black to white is half of what makes a line
;   readable; reversing it is what reads as wrong. Sung default is red
;   (232,42,72); for blue use wR=32 wG=112 wB=240. b* is the unsung gradient,
;   w* the sung one, cBaseB and cWipeB the two outline colours.
;
; RULES, breaking these breaks the template
;   - No "keeptags": it prints furigana pipes as literal text.
;   - No retime() inside a "template line" body: that body runs once PER
;     SYLLABLE, so retime compounds. retime() belongs in "pre-line".
;   - Every \t inside a retimed template needs +foff, because retime moves the
;     line start and \t is measured from it.
;   - Inline colours are 6-digit &HBBGGRR&; the style table uses 8-digit.
;   - The loop count in the Effect field must be >= nbands.
;   - Keep Alignment at 4. The horizontal maths takes the line's left edge from
;     the margin, not from its own measured width.
;   - Use the style's Spacing field, not \fsp. Spacing is included in the
;     measured syllable positions; \fsp is invisible to them and desynchronises
;     the sweep from the text.
; ============================================================================
